questions.q:
In one month, a State faces three problems:
(i) a rise in thefts in its towns;
(ii) a plan to build a new atomic power station in the State;
(iii) a dispute with a neighbouring country over a river.
For each, say which government's list in the chapter's table covers it, name the function, and name the executive head of that government.

Compare and analyse the executive of the Central Government and of a State Government, using the chapter's table. Write one point under each heading:
(a) the nominal head;
(b) the executive head;
(c) two functions found only on that government's list;
(d) a function found on both lists;
(e) how a law made by the Central government is put into practice in a State.
